<p>I really like it, although the last addendum doesn't add anything. The &quot;ten thousand years in the fire&quot; definitely feels like the culmination to me. The description of the phenomenon in the exploration log and interview is what sells it, I think that's well written. The surrounding story with the mine owners etc also feels well though out - not too much, not too little.</p>
<p>So, there are immortal people down in the shaft, either the original lost miners or people who crawled out of the natural tunnel straight from hell. On at least one occasion something crawled up the emergency shaft. And one of the local villagers recently disappeared. You might think we need a perimeter to keep people out of the area. I say we need a perimeter to keep things in as well?</p>
<p>Local villager #4567: &quot;Oh you guys really beefed up the security in the area, lots of dangers with a collapse eh? But who's that guy crawling down the hill, looks like he's on fire??&quot;<br />
Guard: &quot;Don't worry about it, here have some candy.&quot;</p>

